@Fangliding

SOCKS is the internal exit behind my backhaul tunnels. The other server sends mux traffic through those tunnels to the SOCKS inbound, where DispatchLink hands the connection writer to mux. Concurrent mux responses then share that writer without synchronization.

This caused sustained ~95–100% CPU at only 80–120 KB/s, starving other services. Serializing the SOCKS response writes fixed the reproduced race; exit CPU stayed below 4% during a 20-minute production observation.
